### ========================================================================
### Choira MusicTech Assessment - API Testing Suite
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client / Thunder Client / Postman
### ========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Health Check
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authentication APIs (MySQL)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Register New User (Positive Case)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Vedant Kandekar",
    "email": "vedant@example.com",
    "password": "Password123"
}

### 1.2 Register Duplicate Email (Negative Case - Expected 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Duplicate User",
    "email": "vedant@example.com",
    "password": "Password123"
}

### 1.3 Register Validation Failure (Negative Case - Expected 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "",
    "email": "invalid-email",
    "password": "123"
}

### 1.4 Login User (Positive Case)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "vedant@example.com",
    "password": "Password123"
}

### 1.5 Login with Wrong Password (Negative Case - Expected 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "vedant@example.com",
    "password": "WrongPassword123"
}

### 1.6 Get Current User Profile (GET /api/auth/me)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.7 Update User Profile (PUT /api/auth/profile)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Vedant K. (Lead Backend Dev)"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Project Management APIs (MySQL)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Create Project 1 (Active)
# @name createProject1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Choira Audio Processing Engine",
    "description": "High performance audio rendering backend service",
    "status": "active"
}

### 2.2 Create Project 2 (Completed)
# @name createProject2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Music Creator Portal MVP",
    "description": "Creator studio web dashboard",
    "status": "completed"
}

### 2.3 Get All Projects for Authenticated User
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.4 Get Specific Project by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.5 Update Project (PUT /api/projects/:id)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Choira Audio Processing Engine v2",
    "status": "active"
}

### 2.6 Delete Project (PUT /api/projects/:id - Cascades tasks in Mongo)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/2
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Task Management APIs (MongoDB)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Create Task 1 (High Priority, Todo)
# @name createTask1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "projectId": 1,
    "title": "Design MongoDB Aggregation Pipeline for Streams",
    "description": "Calculate track analytics and creator dashboard stats",
    "status": "todo",
    "priority": "high",
    "dueDate": "2026-10-30T18:30:00.000Z"
}

### 3.2 Create Task 2 (Medium Priority, In Progress)
# @name createTask2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "projectId": 1,
    "title": "Implement Redis Cache for User Audio Profiles",
    "description": "Cache artist bio and track listings",
    "status": "in_progress",
    "priority": "medium"
}

### 3.3 Create Task 3 (Low Priority, Completed)
# @name createTask3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "projectId": 1,
    "title": "Configure Docker compose for MySQL & MongoDB",
    "description": "Set up multi-container local development",
    "status": "completed",
    "priority": "low"
}

### 3.4 Create Task with Non-existent Project (Negative Case - Expected 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "projectId": 99999,
    "title": "Unauthorized Project Task",
    "status": "todo"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Filtering and Pagination APIs
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Get Tasks with Default Pagination (Page 1, Limit 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.2 Filter Tasks by Status = 'todo' and Priority = 'high' (Assessment Requirement Example)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?page=1&limit=10&status=todo&priority=high
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.3 Filter Tasks by Specific Project (projectId = 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?projectId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.4 Keyword Search in Task Title
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?search=Redis
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Single Task CRUD Operations
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Get Single Task (Replace ID with actual MongoDB ObjectId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{createTask1.response.body.data.task._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5.2 Update Task Status to 'completed'
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{createTask1.response.body.data.task._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "status": "completed",
    "priority": "high"
}

### 5.3 Delete Single Task
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{createTask1.response.body.data.task._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

